Example: allow a specific role from another account.

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "SpecificRoleTrust",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/DeploymentRole"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}



Custom trust with External ID

A common third-party access pattern:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "ThirdPartyTrust",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/ThirdPartyRole"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "sts:ExternalId": "my-company-12345"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

Use when: you need conditions, specific principals, external IDs, or other trust relationships that the basic console wizard doesn't express conveniently